# =============================================================
# Dependencies — reinstalled from package.json via `npm install`,
# never committed. Regenerating these is fast; storing them bloats
# the repo with thousands of third-party files that aren't "our" code.
# =============================================================
node_modules/

# =============================================================
# Environment / secrets — .env holds machine-specific config
# (e.g. TRACKER_DATA_DIR, PORT). Never commit real secrets; only
# .env.example (a template with no real values) is tracked.
# =============================================================
.env
.env.local

# =============================================================
# Personal data — THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT LINE IN THIS FILE.
# The actual data directory (D:\tracker-system\Tracker) must never
# enter Git history: it holds real financial figures and personal
# logs. If the data folder ever lives *inside* the repo folder by
# accident, this pattern keeps it out regardless of exact path.
# =============================================================
Tracker/
**/Tracker/
*.data/

# =============================================================
# OS / editor noise — machine-specific files with zero project value.
# =============================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# =============================================================
# Logs — runtime output, not source code.
# =============================================================
*.log
npm-debug.log*